{"id":462,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"I theorize that a special magnetic field influenced this Pokémon, changing its molecular structure and causing it to evolve. It emits strange radio waves toward space from its antenna."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"It’s thought that a special magnetic field changed the molecular structure of this Pokémon’s body, and that’s what caused the Pokémon’s evolution."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Some say that Magnezone receives signals from space via the antenna on its head and that it’s being controlled by some mysterious being."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"There are still people who believe that this Pokémon came from outer space. It emanates a powerful magnetic field."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"It uses radar to monitor its territory. Intruders are quickly disposed of with a hyper beam."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"As it zooms through the sky, this Pokémon seems to be receiving signals of unknown origin, while transmitting signals of unknown purpose."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Three units generate magnetism. There have been many mistaken reports of UFO sightings when Magnezone flies through the night sky."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It evolved from exposure to a special magnetic field. Three units generate magnetism."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","White 2","Black 2"],"text":"Sometimes the magnetism emitted by Magnezone is too strong, making them attract each other so they cannot move."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"A group tried to use scientific means to make Magnezone evolve, but their efforts ended in failure."},{"games":["SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"Exposure to a special magnetic field changed MAGNETON’s molecular structure, turning it into MAGNEZONE."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Magnet Pull","hidden":false,"description":"Prevents Steel-type Pokémon from fleeing by pulling them in with magnetism."},{"name":"Sturdy","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon cannot be knocked out by a single hit as long as its HP is full. One-hit KO moves will also fail to knock it out."},{"name":"Analytic","hidden":true,"description":"Boosts the power of the Pokémon's move if it is the last to act that turn."}],"eggGroups":["Mineral"],"genderRate":-1,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":null,"color":"Gray","shape":"Arms","evolution":{"id":81,"name":"Magnemite","condition":null,"children":[{"id":82,"name":"Magneton","condition":"Lv. 30","children":[{"id":462,"name":"Magnezone","condition":"Level up at Mt. Coronet (or 5 other places) or Use Thunder Stone","children":[]}]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,33],[1,48],[1,84],[1,86],[1,161],[1,243],[1,602],[1,604],[12,486],[16,360],[20,209],[24,103],[28,393],[34,430],[40,435],[46,319],[52,113],[58,199],[64,192]],"machine":[776,34,268,451,109,38,598,604,486,527,203,263,430,416,356,360,912,484,270,63,334,442,113,319,182,240,115,156,201,214,796,164,241,916,129,36,851,87,86,85,521,528],"egg":[],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"me1-47","name":"Magnezone","set":"Mega Evolution","date":"2025-09-26","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"47","artist":null,"img":"me1/47"},{"id":"sv8-60","name":"Magnezone","set":"Surging Sparks","date":"2024-11-08","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"60","artist":null,"img":"sv8/60"},{"id":"sv3-65","name":"Magnezone","set":"Obsidian Flames","date":"2023-08-11","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"65","artist":"Anesaki Dynamic","img":"sv3/65"},{"id":"sv1-65","name":"Magnezone ex","set":"Scarlet & Violet","date":"2023-03-31","rarity":"Double Rare","number":"65","artist":"hncl","img":"sv1/65"},{"id":"sv1-226","name":"Magnezone ex","set":"Scarlet & Violet","date":"2023-03-31","rarity":"Ultra Rare","number":"226","artist":"PLANETA Tsuji","img":"sv1/226"},{"id":"swsh12pt5gg-GG18","name":"Magnezone","set":"Crown Zenith Galarian Gallery","date":"2023-01-20","rarity":"Trainer Gallery Rare Holo","number":"GG18","artist":"Shinya Komatsu","img":"swsh12pt5g